[¶](https://wiki.snapmaker.com/en/Snapmaker_Luban/manual/2_supported_gcode_references#g92-set-position)
 G92 - Set Position
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### [¶](https://wiki.snapmaker.com/en/Snapmaker_Luban/manual/2_supported_gcode_references#description-10)
 Description

*   Set the current position to the values specified, and the software endstops are adjusted to preserve the physical movement limits. Thus, you could use `G92` to set the middle of the bed to (0,0,0) and then run .gcode.

### [¶](https://wiki.snapmaker.com/en/Snapmaker_Luban/manual/2_supported_gcode_references#notes-6)
 Notes

*   Incompatible with `G92.1`.

### [¶](https://wiki.snapmaker.com/en/Snapmaker_Luban/manual/2_supported_gcode_references#usage-10)
 Usage

    G92 [E<pos>] [X<pos>] [Y<pos>] [Z<pos>]

Copy

*   Parameters
    *   E: New extruder position.
    *   X: New X axis position.
    *   Y: New Y axis position.
    *   Z: New Z axis position.

### [¶](https://wiki.snapmaker.com/en/Snapmaker_Luban/manual/2_supported_gcode_references#examples-10)
 Examples

*   Specify that the nozzle’s current X position is 10 and the current extruder position is 90.
    
        G92 X10 E90
    
    Copy
    
*   Specify that the nozzle’s current XYZ position is 0, 0, 0.
    
        G92 X0 Y0 Z0
    
    Copy
    

[¶](https://wiki.snapmaker.com/en/Snapmaker_Luban/manual/2_supported_gcode_references#g1029-sm20-operations-related-to-auto-bed-leveling)
 G1029 (SM2.0) - Operations Related To Auto Bed Leveling
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### [¶](https://wiki.snapmaker.com/en/Snapmaker_Luban/manual/2_supported_gcode_references#description-11)
 Description

*   Operations related to automatic bed leveling.

### [¶](https://wiki.snapmaker.com/en/Snapmaker_Luban/manual/2_supported_gcode_references#notes-7)
 Notes

*   In general, it is recommended that users perform automatic bed leveling through the calibration page on the screen, rather than directly using the `G1029` command.
*   In the current version, the operation of directly using the `G1029` command is only applicable to Single Extrusion 3DP.

### [¶](https://wiki.snapmaker.com/en/Snapmaker_Luban/manual/2_supported_gcode_references#usage-11)
 Usage

    G1029 [P<numbers>] [A] [S]

Copy

*   Parameters
    *   P: Set the number of leveling grid points, which can be set within the range of integers \[1, 11\].
    *   A: Enable automatic detection in automatic bed leveling and wait for it to complete.
    *   S: Save the data of automatic bed leveling.

### [¶](https://wiki.snapmaker.com/en/Snapmaker_Luban/manual/2_supported_gcode_references#examples-11)
 Examples

*   You can refer to the following example for automatic bed leveling.
    
        G1029 P3     ; set grid points: 3x3
        G1029 A      ; Enable automatic detection and wait for it to complete.
        G91          ; Set relative position mode
        G0 Z-0.2     ; Manually adjust the Z-axis position
        G0 Z-0.1     ; Repeat until the nozzle is just close to the surface of the bed.
        G1029 S      ; save
    
    Copy
    

[¶](https://wiki.snapmaker.com/en/Snapmaker_Luban/manual/2_supported_gcode_references#m3m4-modified-cnclaser-on)
 M3/M4 (Modified) - CNC/Laser On
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### [¶](https://wiki.snapmaker.com/en/Snapmaker_Luban/manual/2_supported_gcode_references#description-12)
 Description

*   For laser toolheads, both `M3` and `M4` are used to set the laser power.
    *   `M3` is used to set a constant power. That is, in `M3` mode, the machine will not change the laser power during motion.
    *   `M4` is used to set a variable power. That is, in `M4` mode, the machine will dynamically adjust the laser power based on the movement speed of the toolhead during motion, in pursuit of better and smoother laser engraving effects.
*   For CNC toolhead, both `M3` and `M4` are used to set the CNC spindle speed, and the effects of `M3` and `M4` are consistent in the current version.
*   In the current version, the CNC toolheads include the 50W CNC (also known as the standard CNC) and the 200W CNC.

### [¶](https://wiki.snapmaker.com/en/Snapmaker_Luban/manual/2_supported_gcode_references#notes-8)
 Notes

*   For laser toolhead, when the `M3`/`M4` command is used without parameters, the laser toolhead will output at the power configured most recently.
*   For CNC toolhead, when the `M3`/`M4` command is used without parameters, the CNC toolhead will output at the power(or spindle speed) configured most recently.

### [¶](https://wiki.snapmaker.com/en/Snapmaker_Luban/manual/2_supported_gcode_references#usage-12)
 Usage

*   Laser toolhead
    
        M3 [P<%>] [S<pwm>]
        M4 [P<%>] [S<pwm>]
    
    Copy
    
    *   Parameters
        *   P: power, in the \[0, 100\]% range.
        *   S: power, in the PWM \[0, 255\] range.
        *   If both S and P are included, P takes precedence.
*   CNC toolhead
    
        M3 [P<%>] [S<pwm>] [C]
        M4 [P<%>] [S<pwm>] [C]
    
    Copy
    
    *   Parameters
        *   50W CNC
            *   P: power, in the \[0, 100\]% range.
        *   200W CNC
            *   P: spindle speed, in the \[0, 100\]% range.
            *   S: spindle speed, in the \[8000, 18000\]rpm range, usually.
            *   C: Only configure the target spindle speed without turning on the CNC.
            *   If both S and P are included, P takes precedence.

### [¶](https://wiki.snapmaker.com/en/Snapmaker_Luban/manual/2_supported_gcode_references#examples-12)
 Examples

    M3
    M3 P80
    M4 S255

Copy

[¶](https://wiki.snapmaker.com/en/Snapmaker_Luban/manual/2_supported_gcode_references#m5-cnclaser-off)
 M5 - CNC/Laser Off
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### [¶](https://wiki.snapmaker.com/en/Snapmaker_Luban/manual/2_supported_gcode_references#description-13)
 Description

*   Wait for moves to complete, then turn off the spindle/laser power and PWM.

### [¶](https://wiki.snapmaker.com/en/Snapmaker_Luban/manual/2_supported_gcode_references#notes-9)
 Notes

*   `G0` and `G28` will also turn the laser off.

### [¶](https://wiki.snapmaker.com/en/Snapmaker_Luban/manual/2_supported_gcode_references#usage-13)
 Usage

