[¶](https://wiki.snapmaker.com/en/Snapmaker_Luban/manual/2_supported_gcode_references#m425-modified-backlash-compensation)
 M425 (Modified) - Backlash compensation
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### [¶](https://wiki.snapmaker.com/en/Snapmaker_Luban/manual/2_supported_gcode_references#description-46)
 Description

*   Backlash compensation will add extra steps to one or more segments whenever a motor reverses direction. By default, steps are added to the first segment after a direction change. This gives the best dimensional accuracy but may cause marks to appear in the print. Smoothing spreads the added steps over multiple consecutive segments to prevent blemishes in the print, at the expense of dimensional accuracy. In SM2.0, the default method is used, which means that steps are added to the first segment after a direction change.
*   Backlash compensation can be configured at either compile-time or run-time.
*   `MEASURE_BACKLASH_WHEN_PROBING` is not enabled in SM2.0, so the backlash cannot be automatically measured.

### [¶](https://wiki.snapmaker.com/en/Snapmaker_Luban/manual/2_supported_gcode_references#notes-28)
 Notes

*   The default backlash on each axis, i.e., BACKLASH\_DISTANCE\_MM, is 0.
*   The default backlash correction, i.e., BACKLASH\_CORRECTION, is 0.

### [¶](https://wiki.snapmaker.com/en/Snapmaker_Luban/manual/2_supported_gcode_references#usage-46)
 Usage

    M425 [F<value>] [X<linear>] [Y<linear>] [Z<linear>] [B<linear>]

Copy

*   Parameters
    *   F: Enable or disables backlash correction, or sets an intermediate fade-out (0.0 = none; 1.0 = 100%)
    *   X: Set the backlash distance on X (mm; 0 to disable)
    *   Y: Set the backlash distance on Y (mm; 0 to disable)
    *   Z: Set the backlash distance on Z (mm; 0 to disable)
    *   B: Set the backlash distance on B (mm; 0 to disable)

### [¶](https://wiki.snapmaker.com/en/Snapmaker_Luban/manual/2_supported_gcode_references#examples-46)
 Examples

*   Manually configure backlash compensation:
    
        M425 X0.1 Y0.2 Z0.3 ; Set backlash to specific values for all axis
        M425 F1             ; Enable backlash compensation at 100%
    
    Copy
    
*   Report the current backlash configuration:
    
        M425
    
    Copy
    

